{
  "brief_rationale": "The model systematically assessed psychiatric safety (self-harm, aggression, supervision), explicitly recognized residual psychosis and the need for psychiatric follow-up, gave clear antipsychotic safety instructions (no self-adjustment, no double-dosing, confirm with prescriber), stratified cardiac red flags with emergency criteria, used workspace records for order grounding, and formed a concrete executable plan with family receipt. No responsibility-chain error occurred, and at least two high-order points (HO1 and HO2) were completed with case-specific, beyond-minimum actions that shaped the trajectory. This satisfies the Grade 5 boundary.",
